	// kept as its evidence),
	// refused (it stays held: reason says why), missed (this load holds no
	// review at the decision's key, nor one at its place stating what was
	// approved, so it has nothing to release),
	// applied (a prop decision: the load was sent it, and the job that sent it
	// succeeded; the engine reports nothing more of a value, so this doesn't
	// say the property holds it: a document dated after the decision still
	// beats it, and an entity the load doesn't hold takes none),
	// unconfirmed (the job that applies it failed before the engine's word on
	// it was recorded, reason job_failed: the claim may or may not have been
	// written, or the value sent, and no job is coming. Approving it again
	// finishes it while the load still holds the claim's review; choosing a
	// value again finishes a value, and so does the end of the ontology's next
	// job, which sends the load its values again. If the engine wrote the
	// claim before the job failed, that review is gone and there is nothing
	// to approve: the fact is in the load, and the decision stays unconfirmed
	// until another approval of the same document sends it again), or empty:
	// the load read the decision when it was created, and no job has said
	// what became of it.
	// Of a withdraw (an approval taken back, contract 4.16.0): pending while
	// its job has yet to run, withdrawn (what the approval wrote no longer
	// acts: the claim is held again, or, held for a conflict with a document
	// since removed, stays written as its document's statement with no
	// approval to rank it), not_written (the load held nothing the approval
	// wrote), refused (what it wrote stays: differs, quotes an engine before
	// 4.16.0 wrote of several claims of the link keep nothing to tell them
	// apart; too_large; or the backend's document_gone, document_unread,
	// unanswered), or unconfirmed: no word came, so whether it was taken back
	// is not known. With job_failed its job failed, and the end of the
	// ontology's next job sends it again; with document_failed the engine
	// failed its document, and the next approval or take-back in that
	// document sends it again; with not_replayed its document's saved reading
	// can't be reused, so no word can come while this load is current, and
	// the next load won't write the approval.
	// Of a resolve of a name the load links to no one (contract 4.22.0), its
	// word on its own document: pending, written (the load holds what the name
	// held back, as a load read with the decision holds it; with reason
	// not_asked, no review asks about the name now: settled already, by this
	// choice in a run whose word was lost, or by another since), refused
	// (nothing was written in place: reason says why, and the next load
	// applies the choice), unconfirmed (job_failed: choosing again sends it
	// again), or empty for a resolve the load read when it was created. A
	// resolve of a name the load links already (adjudicated, legal_form,
	// part_name, own_name) is unset: the next load applies it. What an alias
	// of the name did in other documents is theirs
	// (FoundryDocumentExtraction.names).
